    "https://nec.peopleadmin.com/postings/7481": {
      "title": "New England College Applicant Portal",
      "description": "New England College Applicant Portal | Admission Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefit Highlights Internal Recruitment Center To see available work study & graduate assistant jobs, use the “Current NEC Employees and Students Log In” then click “search student jobs” Admission Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Admission Counselor Position Purpose This position is tasked with recruiting incoming undergraduate students as part of the overall admissions team. The Admission Counselor is responsible for achieving enrollment goals within an assigned territory and for contributing to the overall success of the department by leading and participating in various recruitment activities. He/she provides personalized communication to prospective students, parents, school counselors and others. Essential Duties Summary Achieve enrollment goals within an assigned territory by communicating with prospective students and parents on a regular basis via telephone, email, social media, personal meetings, and written correspondence; Use the College’s CRM tools to communicate with students and log daily interactions; Deliver small and large group presentations to persuade students to enroll at New England College; Travel to high schools and recruitment fairs to meet with prospective students, parents, and school counselors; Communicate with secondary school counselors, parents, teachers, alumni, coaches, and other key influencers of prospective students; Participate in on-campus and off-campus programs hosted by the College to recruit students; Work with NEC faculty and staff to participate in providing information to prospective students; Write correspondence for print, email, social media, and other platforms as part of a total promotional plan for admissions; Collect and analyze data as part of ongoing assessment of recruitment, and provide enrollment forecasts. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required Experience in undergraduate admission or related positions Excellent written and oral communication skills High-energy disposition, goal-oriented work style, strong customer service orientation Ability to travel extensively Valid driver’s license Preferred Qualifications EEO Statement New England College prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed or religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, veteran’s status or disability in regard to treatment, access to or employment in its programs and activities, in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), individuals with disabilities needing accommodation should contact the ADA Compliance Officer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S00687P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Starting Salary Salary Grade Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you live in CA, CO, NY, NJ or WA? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Henniker Campus 98 Bridge Street Henniker, NH 03242 603.428.2000 Contact Us: hr@nec.edu | 603-428-2359 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
