    "https://nec.peopleadmin.com/postings/7484": {
      "title": "New England College Applicant Portal | DBA Program Director",
      "description": "New England College Applicant Portal | DBA Program Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefit Highlights Internal Recruitment Center To see available work study & graduate assistant jobs, use the “Current NEC Employees and Students Log In” then click “search student jobs” DBA Program Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title DBA Program Director Position Purpose The DBA Program Director is a leadership position responsible for the growth, strategic direction, and effective management of the Executive DBA program. This 12-month hybrid role combines academic leadership with operational oversight, with a strong focus on curriculum development, accreditation, and student success. Key responsibilities include advancing faculty development, mentoring and supporting students, strengthening academic quality, and cultivating strategic partnerships with industry and external stakeholders. The Program Director plays a central role in ensuring the program’s continued growth, relevance, and alignment with institutional and professional standards. The DBA Program Director reports directly to the Dean of the Management Division. Essential Duties Summary Collaborate with the Dean of Management on strategic initiatives, resource allocation, and the development and growth of the Executive DBA program. Supervise program activities, promote communication among leadership, faculty, and students, and resolve operational issues. Manage operations of the Executive DBA program, including scheduling, faculty administration, and student experience across various delivery formats. Mentor and support Executive DBA faculty, ensuring academic quality, innovation, and consistency across program courses. Develop and update courses, including targeted in-person delivery of the online and Henniker campus executive doctoral residency content and experiences. Guide students on academics, practical training, and career growth. Oversee consulting and research projects as part of practical training. Support accreditation and program assessment efforts by utilizing data to promote ongoing improvement. Encourage student-centered initiatives to enhance advising, recruitment, retention, and success. Establish and nurture partnerships with industry and alumni to improve career and educational opportunities. Required Qualifications Education: Terminal degree in a management field along with a related master’s degree. Experience: Demonstrated higher education leadership in roles such as Department Chair or Program Director. Proven experience supporting doctoral program operations, especially in DBA course development, research committee service, and advising doctoral research projects. At least 5 years of successful experience teaching graduate and doctoral-level courses across hybrid, online, and in-person modalities. Skills: Strong leadership, communication, negotiation, and organizational skills. Ability to collaborate across disciplines with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to solve problems and execute plans quickly. Preferred Qualifications Ongoing research and professional development interests. Established industry and employer networks. Grant writing skills and administration. Relevant industry experience and certifications. EEO Statement New England College prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed or religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, veteran’s status or disability in regard to treatment, access to or employment in its programs and activities, in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), individuals with disabilities needing accommodation should contact the ADA Compliance Officer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S00686P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Starting Salary Salary Grade Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you live in CA, CO, NY, NJ or WA? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Henniker Campus 98 Bridge Street Henniker, NH 03242 603.428.2000 Contact Us: hr@nec.edu | 603-428-2359 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
