    "https://nec.peopleadmin.com/postings/7002": {
      "title": "New England College Applicant Portal",
      "description": "New England College Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty - Typography II, Functionality Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefit Highlights Internal Recruitment Center To see available work study & graduate assistant jobs, use the “Current NEC Employees and Students Log In” then click “search student jobs” Adjunct Faculty - Typography II, Functionality Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Faculty - Typography II, Functionality Position Purpose New England College is seeking experienced teachers at the college level to teach introductory and upper level Graphic Design courses. One upper-level graphic design course is currently available for upcoming Spring 2026 second seven weeks semester. Essential Duties Summary In this course students will continue to build on the skills learned in Typography 1. Class discussions, projects and critiques will concentrate on the crucial role of typography and the relationship between type and image in contemporary graphic design. Students will learn advanced techniques for setting type by looking at issues of text type, typographic structure and hierarchy. Required Qualifications This is a digitally-oriented class. Experience with Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign and the Mac operating system is required. Preferred Qualifications Preferred candidates would also have professional design experience. EEO Statement New England College prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed or religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, veteran’s status or disability in regard to treatment, access to or employment in its programs and activities, in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), individuals with disabilities needing accommodation should contact the ADA Compliance Officer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PT00142P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Starting Salary $850 per credit Special Instructions to Applicants Reference Requests Reference Requests Minimum Requests Maximum Requests Cutoff Date Provider Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you live in CA, CO, or WA? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Henniker Campus 98 Bridge Street Henniker, NH 03242 603.428.2000 Contact Us: hr@nec.edu | 603-428-2359 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
