    "https://nec.peopleadmin.com/postings/7476": {
      "title": "New England College Applicant Portal",
      "description": "New England College Applicant Portal | Dean of Health Professions Division Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefit Highlights Internal Recruitment Center To see available work study & graduate assistant jobs, use the “Current NEC Employees and Students Log In” then click “search student jobs” Dean of Health Professions Division Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Dean of Health Professions Division Position Purpose The Dean of the Health Professions Division provides strategic, academic, and administrative leadership for the college’s nursing program and other health professions within the context of a liberal arts education. The Dean is responsible for advancing excellence in teaching, student success, program development, accreditation, faculty leadership, and community partnerships. The Dean works collaboratively with faculty, academic leadership, healthcare partners, and community organizations to prepare graduates who are clinically competent, culturally responsive, and prepared for patient care in a dynamic healthcare environment. Essential Duties Summary Provide vision and strategic direction for undergraduate nursing programs and other healthcare programs. Promote innovative, student-centered teaching and learning with faculty. Lead curriculum development, review, and continuous improvement. Develop new academic programming to meet the needs of the college. Recruit, mentor, and evaluate faculty and staff within the Division. Ensure compliance with state board of nursing requirements and professional accreditation standards. Responsible for writing annual reports as well as accreditation self-studies, and other required reporting, In collaboration with the Associate Dean of Institutional Effectiveness. Work closely with the admissions team for student recruitment, the student success team in relation to retention efforts, progression, and graduation rates. Monitor licensure outcomes, such as the NCLEX -RN Examination pass rates, on a semester basis and implement strategies for continuous improvement. Develop and maintain partnerships with healthcare systems, clinical sites, and community organizations, working to expand clinical placement opportunities. Work to resolve student issues in a timely manner. Collaborate with institutional advancement on fundraising and grant opportunities. Required Qualifications Education Earned doctorate in nursing or a related field (PhD, DNP , or equivalent). Current unencumbered registered nurse (RN) license or eligibility for licensure in the state. Experience 5-7 Years administrative experience in higher education Experience with online and hybrid delivery formats. Evidence of teaching and scholarly or professional attainment. Skills and Knowledge Experience leading accreditation processes with organizations such as the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing. Experience with program development or expansion (e.g., BSN , MSN , or DNP programs). Demonstrated success in building healthcare partnerships and clinical placement networks. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, and administrators. Preferred Qualifications EEO Statement New England College prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed or religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, veteran’s status or disability in regard to treatment, access to or employment in its programs and activities, in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), individuals with disabilities needing accommodation should contact the ADA Compliance Officer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S00659P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Starting Salary Salary Grade Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Henniker Campus 98 Bridge Street Henniker, NH 03242 603.428.2000 Contact Us: hr@nec.edu | 603-428-2359 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://nec.peopleadmin.com/postings/7478": {
      "title": "New England College Applicant Portal",
      "description": "New England College Applicant Portal | Professional Tutor (part-time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefit Highlights Internal Recruitment Center To see available work study & graduate assistant jobs, use the “Current NEC Employees and Students Log In” then click “search student jobs” Professional Tutor (part-time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Professional Tutor (part-time) Position Purpose This part-time position serves as an academic tutor for the Writing and Academic Success Center ( WASC ), providing one-on-one and small group, scheduled and drop-in tutoring sessions to all student populations at New England College. The Professional Tutor works with students, faculty members, success services staff, librarians, mentors, and other members of the New England College community. Essential Duties Summary Provide day-to-day academic support to all student populations at NEC , including students with learning disabilities and students for whom English is not their primary language; Provide general tutoring in such areas as writing development, time-management, study techniques, testing-taking strategies, and goal-setting processes, as well as subject tutoring in the academic disciplines; Promote definable learning strategies which promote academic success and independent learning; Tutor in a variety of settings, including individual, group, drop-in, class-visitation, online, and workshops to all student populations at New England College; Aid in college-wide efforts to promote retention through student academic success and student engagement within the NEC community; Assist with training and overseeing peer (student) tutors; Engage in ongoing training and professional development opportunities; Operate according to established “systems,” general policies and procedures within the WASC and the umbrella of the Student Success Services; Promote and provide additional services within the WASC and the Student Success Services, as well as within the College at large as assigned by the Director; Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in related field; Strong reading, writing, editing, and proofreading skills Knowledge of learning strategies, study skills, and effective academic achievement strategies Excellent interpersonal and communication skills Supervisory skills 2-3 years across all areas: Teaching diverse student populations Teaching with expertise in one or more academic subject areas Working with students with learning differences Working with ESL students Academic counseling/ mentoring/coaching/training/ advising Preferred Qualifications Business, Science, or Math Expertise Master’s degree Library Research Skills EEO Statement New England College prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed or religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, veteran’s status or disability in regard to treatment, access to or employment in its programs and activities, in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), individuals with disabilities needing accommodation should contact the ADA Compliance Officer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S00683P Open Date 08/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Starting Salary Salary Grade Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Henniker Campus 98 Bridge Street Henniker, NH 03242 603.428.2000 Contact Us: hr@nec.edu | 603-428-2359 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
